# default ignore
.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.obsidian/
chroma_db/

# MyST build outputs
_build
.vscode/
dep/

# Generated lab-ready protocol artifacts (rebuilt at deploy; never committed) — see issue #10
**/generated/

# Notion export artifacts (raw exports, zips, staging dirs)
**/resources/*.zip
**/resources/notion_export/
**/resources/Private & Shared*/
**/resources/*-notion.md

# DevNote numbered export folders (e.g. 09-cx43_cell/) — raw exports, never committed
**/resources/[0-9][0-9]-*/

# Staging and scratch — never committed. Staging documents live in tmp/staging/;
# tmp/README.md declares that, and is the one tracked file here because the
# staging skill reads it to find the location. Ignoring the directory itself
# (`tmp/`) would stop git descending into it, so the negation below would never
# fire and the declaration would silently go untracked.
tmp/*
!tmp/README.md
